From f2cbf182f924bb2d8a359fde7e62f3eee1285565 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:01:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] steam-frame client: submit the server's depth grid as a depth
 layer (positional reprojection)

The client advertises CLIENT_CAPABILITY_DEPTH_GRID when the runtime offers
XR_KHR_composition_layer_depth (FRAME_CLIENT_DEPTH_GRID=0 turns it off). Grids
arrive as DepthGrid chunks (UDP datagrams flagged as render poses with a DRGD
magic, or TCP DepthGrid records) and are assembled per eye. Each frame with a
fresh grid for both eyes, the grid is written as standard Z into a grid x grid
depth swapchain per eye and chained on the projection views; the stamp then
carries the rendered eye position so the compositor warps translation per
pixel. A stale grid, or a runtime that refuses the depth, falls back to the
rotation-only stamp.
---
